# oracle: compute hma (u p cv) on a cut-down example (examples/PACKAGES/hma: fcc lj/smooth/linear 3, nvt at 1.0), 108 atoms, 200 steps, sites at the start; native: b332f28 (installed lmp)
# Measured with native LAMMPS: a traced build (compute_hma.cpp per-pair print, b332f28) gave phi_sum 18.113509506451816 at step 50; the engine matches it exactly once the Hessian table uses native dljcut (= -dphiRc). Compared at rel 1e-10 (the residual before the sign fix was 5.5e-8 on c_hma[3]); case runs in about 0.4 s.
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-12
units           lj
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 1.0
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
pair_style      lj/smooth/linear 3
pair_coeff      * * 1.0 1.0
compute         p all pressure NULL pair
velocity        all create 0.1 45678 dist gaussian
fix             settemp all nvt temp 1.0 1.0 0.5
compute         hma all hma settemp u p 9.579586686264458 cv
timestep        0.005
thermo_style    custom step pe temp c_hma[1] c_hma[2] c_hma[3] c_p
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
run             200
